@startuml implementation-issue-states
' cumin works - states of an implementation issue.
' A state is a label on GitHub. "do /" in a state says what goes on while the issue has the label.
' A transition is written as in UML: trigger [guard] / effect. The row of issue-states.md stands in
' parentheses at the end. I9 and I11 change no state; they are notes.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / the Planner or the Owner writes the issue

state "cumin/status/ready" as Ready
Ready : do / wait for a free slot

state "cumin/status/implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the Implementer works

state "cumin/status/awaiting-checks" as Checks
Checks : do / the required checks run

state "cumin/status/reviewing" as Reviewing
Reviewing : do / the Reviewer reviews

state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-review" as OwnerReview
OwnerReview : do / the Owner reviews the pull request

state "cumin/status/awaiting-owner-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Owner answers

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : the Owner adds cumin/status/ready
Ready --> Implementing : poll [ready is the Owner's,\nblockers closed, slot free]\n/ request the implementation (I1)
Implementing --> Checks : Implementer run ended\n[done, pull request verified]\n/ add the closing link (I2)
Implementing --> Decision : Implementer run ended\n[blocked, not verified,\nor second abnormal end]\n/ write the reason, notify the Owner (I2)
Checks --> Reviewing : required checks passed\n/ request the review (I3)
Checks --> Implementing : a required check failed\n[fix requests under the limit]\n/ request a check fix (I4)
Checks --> Decision : a required check failed\n[fix requests at the limit]\n/ notify the Owner (I4)
Checks --> Implementing : pull request conflicts\n/ request a conflict resolution (I14)
Checks --> Decision : wait time passed\n[a required check has no result]\n/ notify the Owner (I15)
Reviewing --> Implementing : Reviewer run ended\n[changes requested,\nrounds under the limit]\n/ request a review fix (I5)
Reviewing --> [*] : Reviewer run ended\n[approved, checks passed, risk/low]\n/ merge, close the issue (I6)
Reviewing --> OwnerReview : Reviewer run ended\n[approved, checks passed,\nrisk/medium or risk/high]\n/ notify the Owner (I7)
Reviewing --> Decision : Reviewer run ended\n[changes requested,\nrounds at the limit]\n/ request the cause, notify the Owner (I8)
Reviewing --> Decision : Reviewer run ended\n[blocked, or no review twice]\n/ post the reason, notify the Owner (I10)
Reviewing --> Checks : Reviewer run ended\n[head commit moved, or\na check does not pass] (no row)
OwnerReview --> [*] : the Owner approved the head commit\n[checks passed]\n/ merge, close the issue (I12)
OwnerReview --> Implementing : the Owner requested changes\n/ request a response (I13)
OwnerReview --> Implementing : pull request conflicts\n/ request a conflict resolution (I14)
OwnerReview --> Ready : the Owner adds cumin/status/ready
Decision --> Ready : the Owner adds cumin/status/ready

note "In every state: the labels of the issue differ from\nthose of its pull request / copy the labels (I11)." as I11
note "After the issue closed with a merged pull request:\n/ write the follow-up note (I9)." as I9

legend right
  A box is a state: a label on GitHub. "do /" is what goes on in the state.
  An arrow is a transition: trigger [guard] / effect.
  In parentheses: the row of issue-states.md today.
endlegend

@enduml
